      {
        "title": "`lib/audit-detail.ts::auditDetailParts` — the audit-column renderer; 10+ untested branches",
        "content": "\n```ts\n// lib/audit-detail.test.ts\nimport { describe, expect, it } from \"vitest\";\nimport { auditDetailParts, auditDetailLine, auditNote } from \"@/lib/audit-detail\";\n// entry factory: makeEntry({ action, detail }) with required AuditEntry fields\n\nit(\"returns [] for a detail object with no recognized keys\", () => {});\nit(\"collapses proposedValue/chosenValue into one 'from → to' part when they differ\", () => {});\nit(\"shows only chosenValue when proposed equals chosen\", () => {});\nit(\"ignores non-string values for string fields (type guard)\", () => {\n  // detail: { externalId: 123 } — num-typed key under str() must be dropped, not stringified\n});\nit(\"ignores NaN/Infinity for numeric fields (Number.isFinite guard)\", () => {\n  // detail: { confidence: Infinity }\n});\nit(\"maps count noun by action (conflict_detected -> 'conflicts', auto_applied -> 'resolutions')\", () => {});\nit(\"falls back to a bare count when the action has no noun mapping\", () => {});\nit(\"renders 'was <previous>' with underscores turned to hyphens\", () => {\n  // detail: { previousStatus: \"auto_applied\" } -> \"was auto-applied\"\n});\nit(\"auditDetailLine returns null (not empty string) when there is nothing to render\", () => {});\nit(\"auditNote returns null for an empty-string note\", () => {});\n```\n\n",
